a human tragedy of unspeakable  proportions unfolded in the night of the  19th to 20th of April of the Libyan  coast south of lamb producer the  combined effort of rescue teams from  Italy and Malta could only save 27 lives  out of an estimated 800 people including  many women and children a few days  before 400 migrants died in another  shipwreck Donald Tusk the president of  the european council declared that it  cannot continue like this we cannot  accept that hundreds of people died when  trying to cross the sea to Europe this  is why I have decided to call an  extraordinary european council this  thursday the summit will discuss at the  highest EU level what more you member  states and EU institutions can do  together concretely and immediately the  first priority is to save lives EU  leaders will discuss how to rapidly  reinforce operation try it on with more  rescue teams more vessels and  helicopters and a wider area of  operation member states must also look  at how best to provide international  protection to those in the region who  need it and how to better organize the  return home of unauthorized economic  migrants it is also urgent to stop the  criminal networks of smugglers and  traffickers who earn money by exploiting  desperate migrants leaders will explore  ways to do this including the possible  destruction of traffickers boats with  military means based on the experience  of counter-piracy operation Atalanta of  the somali coast i do not expect any  quick fix solutions to the root causes  of migration because Stalin had they  existed we would have used them long ago  it concerns all of us all of Europe  that's why we need to act and act  together now  you
 

